{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310631,"nonce":"YMQnmb/GSCpeLHEJA3cEEcYTpIY=","title":"RESOLVED by `1f2d34bc` — the site was `expr/call/direct.rs::try_resolved_function_call`,","message":"**RESOLVED by `1f2d34bc` — the site was `expr/call/direct.rs::try_resolved_function_call`,\nwhich emitted the call and never filled defaults.**\n\n**THE DURABLE LESSON:** `cranelift_backend.rs` (~3662) PADS AN UNDER-ARITY CALL\nWITH ZERO rather than trapping, and says so in its own comment. That is why a\nmissing default became a silent `0` instead of a loud failure, and why the MIR\ndump misled: the call left the builder with 2 args against a 3-parameter\nsignature and the backend supplied the third. A probe in `build_call_direct`\n(`emitted_args=2 declared=3`) is what proved it; no dump shows this.\nThat padding remains a standing silent-wrong-answer generator for any lowering\npath that forgets to fill defaults.\n\n---\n\n---\nname: bugs-instance-method-optional-args-ignored\ndescription: \"RESOLVED 1f2d34bc. The site was direct.rs::try_resolved_function_call. THE LESSON: cranelift pads under-arity calls with ZERO, so a missing argument never fails loudly.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n---\n\n**An instance method's default parameter value never arrives.** Statics are\ncorrect as of 30e022aa; instance calls are not.\n\n```haxe\nclass M {\n    public function new() {}\n    public function trail(a:Int, ?b:String) return \"trail \" + a + \"/\" + b;\n    public function trailDef(a:Int, b:String = \"dflt\") return \"trailDef \" + a + \"/\" + b;\n    public function lead(?a:Int, b:String) return \"lead \" + a + \"/\" + b;\n    static function main() {\n        var m = new M();\n        Sys.println(m.trail(1));      // \"trail 1/\"          CORRECT (b is null)\n        Sys.println(m.trailDef(2));   // \"trailDef 2/\"       WRONG, want 2/dflt\n        Sys.println(m.lead(\"z\"));     // \"lead 45164878144/\" WRONG, want 0/z\n    }\n}\n```\n\n\nProbe with `RAYZOR_DEFAULTS_DEBUG=1` (shipped b15effc3) and\n`RAYZOR_DUMP_MIR=1` (PRE-optimisation).\n\n1. The MIR signature is correct:\n   `fn @M.trailDef [name=trailDef]($0: *void, $1: i32, $2: string)`.\n2. PRE-opt MIR emits **three** arguments, the third a zero:\n   `$21 = const 2i32 / $22 = const 0i64 / $23 = call fn3($20, $21, $22)`.\n   Arity is right; the VALUE is wrong. `\"dflt\"` is never built.\n3. The path taken is `expr/call/direct.rs::try_resolved_function_call`\n   (`let arg_regs: Vec\u003c_\u003e = if *is_method`). Confirmed by probe:\n   `[direct] trailDef id=IrFunctionId(3) is_method=true hir_args=2`.\n4. **HIR carries only TWO args** (`this`, `2`). So the third is added between\n   that point and the emitted instruction.\n5. `fill_default_args` is NEVER CALLED for this function -- the\n   RAYZOR_DEFAULTS_DEBUG line never prints for it. That is why the default is\n   absent rather than merely mis-ordered.\n6. `build_call_direct` (builder.rs ~348) does NOT pad; it only TRUNCATES, and\n   only for externs.\n\nSo: who turns 2 argument registers into 3? Look at\n`maybe_materialize_for_call`, at `build_call_direct_with_type_args`\n(builder.rs ~636), and at whether a later re-resolution replaces the\ninstruction. Once found, call `bind_skipped_optional_args` then\n`fill_default_args` there, both with `has_implicit_this = true`.\n\n\n- `expr/call/mod.rs` instance branch\n- `expr/call/resolved_method.rs` \"[Field method]\" branch\n- adding `fill_default_args` to the above\n\nRelated: [[bugs-irfunctionid-is-module-local]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_instance_method_optional_args_ignored` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}